title: The Linke Reviews the Coalition
view-if: in_left_front and (linke_review_timer = 0 or ((welfare_goal = 0 or welfare_goal_completed) and (economy_goal = 0 or economy_goal_completed) and (finance_goal = 0 or finance_goal_completed) and (labor_goal = 0 or labor_goal_completed) and (foreign_goal = 0 or foreign_goal_completed) and (reichswehr_goal = 0 or reichswehr_goal_completed))) and linke_demands_seen = 1 and linke_review_seen = 0 and spd_in_government
on-arrival: {!
Q.linke_review_seen = 1;
Q.linke_demands_met = 1;
Q.linke_score = 6;
var goals = ['welfare', 'agriculture', 'economy', 'finance', 'labor', 'foreign', 'reichswehr'];
for (var g of goals) {
    if (Q[g + '_goal'] && !Q[g + '_goal_completed']) {
        Q.linke_demands_met = 0;
        Q.linke_score -= 1;
    }
}
!}
new-page: true
tags: event
go-to: goals_success if linke_demands_met; goals_failed if not linke_demands_met

= The Linke Reviews the Coalition

At the start of this government, the Linke set out its demands:

[? if welfare_goal = 1 : - Raise the Grundsicherung and the pension level: [? if welfare_goal_completed : done ?][? if not welfare_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

[? if economy_goal = 1 : - Public ownership of housing and energy: [? if economy_goal_completed : done ?][? if not economy_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

[? if finance_goal = 1 : - A wealth tax and a higher top rate: [? if finance_goal_completed : done ?][? if not finance_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

[? if labor_goal = 1 : - A higher minimum wage: [? if labor_goal_completed : done ?][? if not labor_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

[? if foreign_goal = 1 : - Peace talks and no new arms exports: [? if foreign_goal_completed : done ?][? if not foreign_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

[? if reichswehr_goal = 1 : - A freeze of the defence budget: [? if reichswehr_goal_completed : done ?][? if not reichswehr_goal_completed: not done ?] ?]

@goals_failed
on-arrival: linke_relation -= 10; workers_spd -= 4; unemployed_spd -= 4

We have not delivered what the Linke asked for. Its party congress votes to leave the coalition, and its leaders accuse us of betraying our own voters.

- @appeal: Ask the Linke for more time.
- @linke_leaves.new_partners: Look for new partners in the centre.
- @linke_leaves.let_it_happen: Let them go.

@appeal
choose-if: linke_score >= 4 and linke_relation > 50 and linke_appeal_seen = 0
unavailable-subtitle: [? if linke_score < 4: They do not believe that we are serious about the coalition's goals. ?] [? if linke_relation <= 50: Our relations are too poor. ?] [? if linke_appeal_seen = 1: We have already asked for more time once. ?]
on-arrival: linke_review_seen = 0; linke_review_timer += 6; linke_appeal_seen = 1

We argue that the laws are on their way and that a left government is worth saving. The Linke gives us six more months.

@goals_success
on-arrival: workers_spd += 4; unemployed_spd += 4; linke_relation += 10; workers_linke += 3; linke_coalition_success += 1; linke_demands_seen = 0; linke_review_seen = 0
achievement: einheitsfront_2

Against the expectations of most commentators, we have delivered on the Linke's demands. The coalition holds, and the Linke will stay in government, still watching for any backsliding.
